        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenji Mizoguchi, David Wall, Kōzaburō Yoshimura\n- Films: Noëlle, An Osaka Story\n- Topics: Japanese film, film directing, screenwriting, film awards\n\nFacts:\n- Kenji Mizoguchi was born on May 16, 1898, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- David Wall is an American actor who wrote, produced, and directed the 2007 dramedy film \"Noëlle.\"\n- The 2007 film \"Noëlle,\" directed by David Wall, won the Best Director Award at the Fort Lauderdale International Film Festival.\n- Kenji Mizoguchi died on August 24, 1956.\n- The 1957 black-and-white Japanese film \"An Osaka Story\" was directed by Kōzaburō Yoshimura.\n- \"An Osaka Story\" was based on a story by Kenji Mizoguchi.",
